    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9e4161c1cce24435b448ebf51b27e119",
      "statement": "HAAPServer state splits between persistent stores (directory, tasks, audit — whichever backing was constructed) and per-process memory: the NonceManager and the _pending_challenges challenge table, both guarded so handler mutations are thread-safe, reset on restart by design; start() runs serve_forever on a ThreadingHTTPServer with daemon_threads in a background thread and returns the bound server (port 0 works for tests), stop() shuts it down, and the built-in server is plain HTTP rather than HTTPS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L461-L472",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:961b2b030f6dabb1881d3da6ceb3dc08839737fb145202d21c99964030ca81be:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L80-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71e8ccb670a7a1024afb131708a1731266f381ce2008de749dc4288a800ac79a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d6b384e8d164047b2ce28f8e4c74fbb",
      "statement": "haap serve (cmd_serve) loads the Identity and Directory from the agent data directory, constructs HAAPServer with a file-backed AuditLog and the --speciality argument, and binds --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8443 by default, printing the three endpoints and sleeping until Ctrl+C calls server.stop(); it wires no on_task executor, marketplace catalog or auto_accept policy, custom notifier or policy, so with defaults inbound task_requests are answered with task_accept and left working, friend requests queue to the ConsoleNotifier according to policy.json, open-services handlers answer with an empty catalog, and no skills or tools are advertised.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/cli.py#L169-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee0499a9705f633bb54bc4b933c7bef16df72254b641219747587d6fa5ae7ca6:"
        },
